prompt:
Write a method named `sumGrid` that takes a 2D `int` array parameter `grid` and returns the sum of all its elements. For example, `sumGrid` called on `{{1, 2}, {3, 4}}` should return `10`.

Complete the method below.

```java
public int sumGrid(int[][] grid) {
    /* your code here */
}
```

sampleResponse:
```java
public int sumGrid(int[][] grid) {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
        for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
            sum += grid[r][c];
        }
    }
    return sum;
}
```

prompt:
Write a method named `rowWithMaxSum` that takes a rectangular 2D `int` array parameter `grid` and returns the index of the row whose elements have the largest sum. For example, for `{{1, 2}, {10, 10}, {0, 1}}`, row 1 has the largest sum (20), so the method should return `1`.

Complete the method below.

```java
public int rowWithMaxSum(int[][] grid) {
    /* your code here */
}
```

sampleResponse:
```java
public int rowWithMaxSum(int[][] grid) {
    int maxRow = 0;
    int maxSum = Integer.MIN_VALUE;
    for (int r = 0; r < grid.length; r++) {
        int rowSum = 0;
        for (int c = 0; c < grid[r].length; c++) {
            rowSum += grid[r][c];
        }
        if (rowSum > maxSum) {
            maxSum = rowSum;
            maxRow = r;
        }
    }
    return maxRow;
}
```

prompt:
Write a method named `diagonalSum` that takes a square 2D `int` array parameter `grid` (the same number of rows and columns) and returns the sum of the elements on its main diagonal (where the row index equals the column index). For example, `diagonalSum` called on `{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}, {7, 8, 9}}` should return `15` (1 + 5 + 9).

Complete the method below.

```java
public int diagonalSum(int[][] grid) {
    /* your code here */
}
```

sampleResponse:
```java
public int diagonalSum(int[][] grid) {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < grid.length; i++) {
        sum += grid[i][i];
    }
    return sum;
}
```
